{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/147047-help-me-build-a-setting","id":147047,"title":"Help me build a setting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-23T13:09:05-07:00","id":147047,"title":"Help me build a setting?","content":"<i>As a quick blurb: I'm putting this post up for two reasons: Firstly, because I welcome feedback and advice from those who have more experience than me in WoD (which basically means any!) and secondly because writing things out helps me think. For those worried about stumbling across spoilers for their own game, my group is based in southern Ontario. If you live here, you might want to think twice about reading on, but otherwise feel free. This might be a good mental exercise for you, or you might suggest good ideas or help me with problems I'll run into creating this setting. I haven't decided whether this post will end with any meaningful spoilers anyways.<br /> <br /> I will try to summerize the actual setting in this doc: </i><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14FUVZX0BRpf214PGPBMiwoeTIfD1D3YdYtiLsmayw34/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> On to the juicy stuff: I want to run a Geist campaign (yes, I'm coming from a D&amp;D background) - eventually. I'll probably run a few short term mortals games first to get my group acquainted with the system, and so I have a basic understanding of the GMC rules when I try to adapt Geist to them. The short term mortal campaigns might also help to establish the setting or some plot points leading up to the actual game, or they can be just one off games with the Mortal system. I want my players to roll up disposable characters for this to get them roleplaying in the new system, but I'm not above having a long and horror driven precursor to becoming Sin Eaters. I've thought about doing this over summer and having the game transition around Halloween just for the extra atmosphere - the game will likely change from out and out horror to dark humour and a touch of anatomical horror.<br /> <br /> My first problem is I am not travelled enough to write about other cities or places, but the local area doesn't really lend itself to urban horror and gang warfare like a city like New York might. I'm not really liking the idea of basing it in Toronto and hearing people make jokes about Rob Ford, or else basing it in another nearby city and having a lot of rural adventures happen (searching through bushes and the like)- so I want to create a fictional city that - while still in Ontario - is a blank slate. The other problem is gun laws - they're much different here and having a gun is fairly out of place - but I'm thinking I'll just have a large black market that makes it so even mortals can get them - albiet illegally. Without them it seems like Mortals would have a hard time becoming interesting NPCs. <br /> <br /> My second problem (or rather, issue I'd like to address) is I'd like to keep my players serious. I'm hoping to do this by mixing in a lot of sobering themes - As part of the plot I plan to stomp on my players emotions just enough to make them want to win. Show them the orphan that is already dead and forgotten due to neglect while the people responsible enjoy carefree lives and get them to do something about it. Any advice in this Vein? Where do I draw the line? <br /> <br /> I intend to continue expanding on this and developing this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T16:27:31-07:00","id":147266,"title":"","content":"1) The thing to do if you don't want to go local is do research. My own campaign is set in New Haven, and I am running other sorts of WoD games in Prague and Malibu/Santa Monica, neither of which I have been to. If you have time for it, do some research on the city. Wikipedia is not a good be-all-end-all but it is a good starting place. I'd also look for sorts of stuff on the web like you think players might frequent. For my current Changeling game I used Yelp to get some local nightclubs, restaurants, and similar. You could also check out Urban Explorers websights, or ghost hunter society websites, for creepy and/or abandoned places.<br /> <br /> 1a) I don't see a connection between Mortals having a gun or not and being interesting NPCs. Some of my most interesting NPCs don't fight at all.<br /> <br /> 2) The only way for this to succeed is for you to discuss things with your players are far as mood and theme you want to maintain. If they are used to goofing around in games simply putting serious stuff in won't change that most of the time. Make your expectations clear and make clear why you have those expectations. if they like levity, work out a compromise so that they can play as they want and be serious when needed. People often try to use system mechanics or just having grim events to drive player behavior, and that tends to lead to frustration for everyone.<br /> <br /> I've never been to Ontario, so lack any specific suggestions for local places/ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T10:38:49-07:00","id":149502,"title":"","content":"I gave it some thought, and I think I'm going to take your advice a little and base it in an existing city - I'm just going to go slightly further away. I've decided to place this in Detroit - which seems like it'll be an amazing setting with all the guns, drugs, death, violence and day of the dead shenanigans I could ask for. Apparently they have a place called Mexicantown - which I can only assume is Detroits version of little Italy or Chinatown - and Dias del los meurtos seems like its a thing there. There also pretty close to the Canadian border so I don't think the culture will be that alien to me. As an added bonus, of all the cities I can think of, Detroit is the only one that I can think of as 'in the process of dying' - a point of which I want to integrate into my setting. I'm thinking it's not just metaphorical death - I'll throw in some God machine mechanisations to help explain how it went from such a thriving city to what it is now.<br /> <br /> I think I need to start thinking about notable NPCs for the area. My thoughts are:<br /> <br /> Krewes - I like the imagery of clowns as sin-eaters, so I'm going to make one Krewe in particular based on this. I want to contrast this away from characters like the Joker and Harley Quinn, but I also like the imagery of a sexy female Harlequin. I also don't like the imagery created by Insane clown posse for this, although they ARE a major gang apparently so perhaps some of their members will be from that area, but others from straight entertainment aspects. I've got three members in mind so far:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>A sexy Harlequin - I'm thinking a lithe black woman with white face paint who is also a skilled acrobat</li> <li>A muscle bound clown who does more of the heavy lifting grunt work - polish background I think</li> <li>A black as night Mime who is the 'speak softly but carry a big stick' leader of the group. I'm thinking his Schtick will be to coat himself in full body paint and perform as a statue - waiting for donations. I'm still deciding what his true ethnicity and history is - but mostly I just want him to be the big bad scary leader that no one really speaks directly to.</li> </ol>Still debating what other Krewes will be in the area. Drugs will probably be a big theme for one, and Religion for another.<br /> <br /> Police - I mentioned before that I want to add Inferno demons - I think the police will be where they make their presence known. Some will be mortals, many will be cultists and a select few will be possessed humans controlled largely by Inferno demons. Mostly, these will be direction-less, in it for the hell raising boys club - I just want the police to actively be the cruel bad guys so far.<br /> <br /> Tengu Corp - of note will be a corporation called Tengu Corp - which will deal with everything from foreclosures to investments in Detroit -a front for the God Machine. I don't want the GM to be a major player in my campaign - but it will be the mostly oblivious backbone that caused all the ruckus. The thinking is that a particularly powerful demon was captured here in the underworld and several angels - along with a large cult - now maintain infrastructure that keeps it mostly contained. The demon itself is not all that dangerous now, but its passive influence is largely to blame for Detroits recent ruin over the last 30 years. I might rename the corperation if I can find a more appropriate real life corperation that helps color Detroits local scene. If it's not obvious by the way: I'm referring to inferno Demon being contained by infrastructure - not GM demons. The infrastructure is like a damn holding a force of nature at bay.<br /> <br /> I think next I need to come up with something to make the setting a bit more colourful and cheerful. I'm really second guessing the whole 'lost and alone' theme - this is starting to feel too depressing. Perhaps I'll make one or two of the other local Krewes a bit friendlier and more cheerful than I originally envisioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1085,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","user":"Oddness","date":". 05-26-2014, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T14:47:26-07:00","id":149731,"title":"","content":"This generally looks like a good start. I hate Inferno with the fire of a thousand suns, but Demon the Decent is very good. If using the God Machine anyway, Decent Demons may work well/better. The only advice I have about including the God Machine in a non-Mortals game (or any not focused on it) is opposing a fundamental aspect of reality itself can make whatever else you are doing seem like small potatoes and take some of the wind from other baddies. It is not necessarily bad, but it is something to be aware of. Some players don't care, some players find it a distraction.<br /> <br /> If you are looking for deeper roleplaying and a deeper game, having helpful NPCs the PCs care about helps. If everyone is against them, the world is a dungeon crawl with more rules.Friendly NPCs can provide romance options (which often make people think about their characters more, I have found) and can be targeted by bad guys since they are probably easier to kill than Sin-Eaters (a T-Rex is easier to kill than a Sin-Eater). You just really, really have to balance that last part. You don't want players worrying about them being potential liabilities.<br /> <br /> I'll note here you need to look a lot into Haunts and ghosts for them to deal with. What you have is cool (and Balance of Shadows, my game, deals with other line stuff a lot) but many of their powers work either best or only with ghosts, and ghosts and haunts are how they get their juice back. You need to be sure to have a good deal of that for them to deal with. Just don't expect most ghosts to be much challenge...all of them can punch a ghost into submission, and if any of Stigmata Key ghosts will be nearly helpless. So plan ghost related challenges more around roleplaying and such than combat, mostly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T14:55:39-07:00","id":149734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">~~I hate Inferno with the fire of a thousand suns,</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh? Why is this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call me Count <img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","name":"123456789blaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T15:05:08-07:00","id":149739,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to spend a lot of time slamming the book, as I try not to do that. On a practical level, I don't feel it does a good job representing Demons in an interesting way. On a less practical level, I thought it was not as good as Demon the Fallen (which is not automatic when I like a Classic WoD game. Masquerade is my favorite Classic WoD game and I like Requiem a lot. Changeling was my second favorite and Lost is tied with Geist for my fave New WoD game. Plus I think Demon the Decent is awesome). If it were more oriented as a &quot;Book of the Possessed&quot; it would not have been so bad, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 05-26-2014, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T16:41:38-07:00","id":149802,"title":"","content":"I don't think that there's really a need to tone done the &quot;lost and alone&quot; though. In a way I think that sense of isolation and alienation is core to what Detroit has become. Especially when you look at the history of racial violence and white flight in the city, there's a great deal of &quot;us vs. them&quot; survival mentality almost bred into the city's bones. <br /> <br /> What Baron Samedi says is all quite true, though I'd argue that there are ways to make the world feel alive and engaging while keeping every powerful NPC an enigmatic and dangerous enemy. It's just a matter of fleshing out the NPCs like people. Maybe they all start out wanting the party dead, but they have their reasons, and with work and negotiation, they can be turned to see the party as assets, allies, or even unlikely friends. <br /> <br /> My personal advice for running a Geist game is to make a bigger bad out there that the sin eaters have to stay concealed from, much like GMC Demons and Angels. Otherwise I find it's really hard for the players and their characters to give even the slightest care towards concealing themselves from the mortal populace... they have no mechanical reason to do so, and almost no fluff written as to why they would do so. Sin Eaters with the right manifestations can shrug off missile strikes, and in the off-chance that you kill them, they'll just get right back up again 24 hours later. It feels like asking Achilles to stay home from battle - the only incentive he has is one of his own making, not fear of his enemies, no matter how numerous. <br /> <br /> P.S. Inferno is wonderful and I think the point of it is that Demons *aren't* interesting... but they give incentive to people, who are interesting, do interesting things. I'd be interested in hearing why you don't like it so much Baron, but this topic I think is not the place to do so. =P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","user":"Anachronistic Jam","date":". 05-26-2014, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T19:43:01-07:00","id":149927,"title":"","content":"The biggest reason to not reveal themselves is privacy, and wanting to get really anything done. In the modern world, they would have international eyes on them if they revealed as having superpowers, not to mention various sorts of supernatural forces eye. It's less the people trying to kill them (which would be a thing) and more not being able to go anywhere or get anything done because of all the people and cameras following them around. It's an incredibly bad idea for anyone who wants to, well, live any sort of life and get anything done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T20:10:05-07:00","id":149964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/147047-help-me-build-a-setting?p=149927#post149927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest reason to not reveal themselves is privacy, and wanting to get really anything done. In the modern world, they would have international eyes on them if they revealed as having superpowers, not to mention various sorts of supernatural forces eye. It's less the people trying to kill them (which would be a thing) and more not being able to go anywhere or get anything done because of all the people and cameras following them around. It's an incredibly bad idea for anyone who wants to, well, live any sort of life and get anything done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially when they <i>already</i> deal with enough severe invasions of their privacy from dead people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T20:21:48-07:00","id":149983,"title":"","content":"See, that's exactly the reason I think they would come out of the closet. Yeah, some sin eaters might think very long term with schemes and continuous plans, but the average person offered a second chance at life? I think &quot;most famous person in the world and revolutionary figure in human history overnight&quot; is a pretty good way to start such a second chance.<br /> <br /> As for living a life and getting things done? Celebrities do just fine, and I think that most of your average sin-eaters goals would actually be much more easily accomplished as a near-messianic figure with celebrity status and the favors that might entail.<br /> <br /> As you say, the various supernatural forces are a threat in a crossover game, but that falls under the auspices of my &quot;make a bigger bad&quot; assertion. I think that the collective displeasure of werewolves/vampires/mages/the godmachine definitely counts as a bigger bad than anything less than a T3 crew; individually, let alone together. Even saying that the US government already knows about them and is pulling a coverup the size of a planet slightly counts, as one Sin-Eater is going to have a hard time punching through that network of misinformation. <br /> I just think it should be clearly established, particularly in the GMs mind beforehand why none, out of the many decadent, charismatic, and attention-hungry sin-eaters that have come before, none have broken the Geist-equivalent of a masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T20:42:25-07:00","id":149996,"title":"","content":"I'm going to stand by Inferno Demons for now - I think fire and brimstone demons compliment guardians of the underworld a bit better than the techno spy game of Descent. Keep in mind that this is early in building the setting - a good start for now with lots of refining required. The god machine will most likely not become a major player in the story very often, and the demon police are there primarily so the players don't feel like the unopposed master race of the universe otherwise. There will be a lot of ghosts, npc sin eaters and mortals to flesh out yet.<br /> <br /> I plan to have plenty of ghosts for the players to look after - who can be threatened to give them a reason to take their jobs seriously. A big bad for them to be scared of also seems like a good idea, but I still have no idea who that will be considering the god machine is tied up suppressing the demon and the demon is suppressed. <br /> <br /> One idea that's still a floating loose thread is that the Inferno gate is actually in the underworld, which begs the question: why and how? Perhaps it's also corrupted the local Kerberos and twisted it into the big bad I need? I guess I could also turn the mortal gangs of Detroit into something to be scared of yet - maybe they know some rituals they shouldn't and have taken it upon themselves to perform very sloppy exorcisms in order to rid the city of the rival gangs (all sin-eaters?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T21:23:22-07:00","id":150021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/147047-help-me-build-a-setting?p=149983#post149983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just think it should be clearly established, particularly in the GMs mind beforehand why none, out of the many decadent, charismatic, and attention-hungry sin-eaters that have come before, none have broken the Geist-equivalent of a masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Attention-hungry.<br /> <br /> The group of people who have enough aggregate lore and rumor to be suspicious of large government and mass media and tend to form into <i>cults.</i><br /> <br /> The group of people who routinely deal with mostly-invisible beings that frequently react negatively to being seen or acknowledged and <i>are sought out by the unquiet dead.</i><br /> <br /> The group of people who <i>categorically have bonded with a secret-keeping mystery-beast from beyond the veil that is <b>always watching their every thought and deed.</b></i><br /> <br /> I find your assessment of the frequency with which such people emerge who can't get enough attention to be suspect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oddness, any plans on looking at urban decay as a theme or motif?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-27-2014, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T21:44:52-07:00","id":150028,"title":"","content":"Back on topic, it's interesting to note that there are vast salt mines and deposites beneath Detroit. Salt, in current occult practices at least, is often used in wards and bans... just what, in the world of darkness, might need to be contained beneath that much; and what might have started leaking out with the mining company's operations? <br /> As for possibly sinister companies, the Illitch family owns a startling number of businesses in and around Detroit. The family was presented the Key to Detroit in 2008. Now, obviously, in the real world there's not much sinister about the family... but this is WoD, and there's always fun to be had with influential, apparently respectable, and incredibly wealthy families. <br /> <br /> Yes. People that form cults tend to be attention-hungry. Maybe not on the grand, celebrity scale, but even then most aren't content to build a cult and say &quot;Y'know what guys? I think we're big enough. I think we've spread the word to as many people as possible and should just sit back now.&quot; <br /> <br /> Errr... most ghosts *want* to be seen and acknowledged. That's the only way they can find resolution or continue the works they had in life. Depending on the lore you're drawing from, their existence can depend on others remembering them. I very much doubt that a ghost who wants to be left alone feels very well served by nobody acknowledging her existence, in as much as a ghost has the agency to &quot;feel&quot; in a conventional sense. <br /> <br /> As for the Geists themselves, they're insane, yes... but secret-keeping? That depends on how you choose to portray them. I think there's plenty of evidence in the book to support that they only appear to keep secrets because they're too mad to really know what's relevant information for their Sin-Eater... and a &quot;Game of Second Chances&quot; applies to both members of the bargain. With the charicterization of many Sin-Eaters as being driven to hedonism, the best place to find that lifestyle is as one of the rich and famous. <br /> ...and what of the benevolent Sin-Eaters, the ones who want to make their abilities known for the medical and scientific breakthroughs they might inspire? Maybe they don't want the celebrity, but being globally famous is the safest way to ensure that you *aren't* packed off to a super-secret lab as a super-secret lab rat. What about the brooding author who's never been published? Become famous and publishers are killing each other for the rights to sell your work... and so on.<br /> <br /> Suspicious of the government and media? I'm not sure what that has to do with anything. Either they have enough evidence of Massive Malevolent Government Conspiracy (tm), which falls under my recommendation above, or they don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T21:53:56-07:00","id":150031,"title":"","content":"One thing you might want to look into is local crime statistics by area: they're a good way to get to get a general layout of the SES of a place, especially if cross-referenced with demographic information (although in Detroit that might be a bit tricky, since the percentage of black people has been rising steadily, since they frequently make up a decent amount of the poor in America, near I can tell, and those who can afford to have tended to leave Detroit. Still potentially useful, though).<br /> <br /> Also, a common...mistake by STs new to WoD: if you want an NPC to be a major antagonist, don't just make them a physical powerhouse. In fact, I'd recommend making them slightly physically weaker than the PCs. WoD isn't like D&amp;D, where (barring the save-vs-die spells), the amount of damage you can do is capped, or is more-or-less easily predictable. If your players know much about the game at all, and if you allow stuff from non-core books like Armory and Armory: Reloaded, they can put out amounts of damage that would, according to the guidelines in the core, totally obliterate vehicles <i>multiple times a turn</i>. And it is much, much easier to stack a characters damage output than it is to stack their ability to soak up damage, unless you give them Attributes or Skills or similar in the 20+ range. Good antagonists in the WoD are hard to deal with either because they can't be found, thus forcing the PCs to capture and interrogate underlings or follow clues, or they can't be attacked in the conventional sense because they're in the public eye and attacking them will bring waay too much heat down on the PCs, or they're not something that can be punched. Golden rule of antagonists: the moment you stat them out and put them in a situation where the players can thwack them, they'll thwack them, and almost certainly thwack them hard.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of a Changeling game I ran once where the weather was going nuts, and the players were tapped to investigate it, eventually discovering, after much legwork, that the problem was that an anti-Fae shield the local Freehold had put up broke the ancient pact between the Seasons and the Fae, so the only way to fix it was to go into deep Arcadia, encountering their old Fae captors in situations that, even with iron, they were near-powerless in, and reforge the pacts to secure the stability of the seasons for the world. If the solution was &quot;find X, thwack X&quot;, then it wouldn't have been nearly so satisfying or interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T22:44:13-07:00","id":150044,"title":"","content":"I'll note something else I do, may be helpful.<br /> <br /> I often tend to have fewer &quot;villains&quot; and more, to borrow a fellow ST's term, &quot;agendad NPCs&quot; Agendad NPCs are trying to do something. They have a plan, which they are carrying out. The PCs may decide to help, oppose, or ignore them. But more often then not, an agenda's NPC has other Agendad NPCs they are eventually going to clash with. It's a thing. Unless the players ignore them, they will eventually clash with one or the other. I like the situation because it gives the players the flexibility to make the decision of who to back, and puts the onus on them to find out what the Agendad NPCs true goals are...they could wind up working for someone who seems pretty friendly but is pretty nasty.<br /> <br /> Now, I do have some outright villains, who will not work with the PCs for any reason. But I try to have a reason for that beyond &quot;the are evil&quot; Ivory Claws, from among the Pure, could be good villians due to their hatred of Necromancy, and the inbreeding and abuse are just more reasons to hate them. A Keberoi could work as well. Looking at the (excellent, BTW) post above mine, a Keberoi could fill the place of &quot;true fae&quot; here.<br /> <br /> A few books have some ideas for stuff that may not be where you would think to. <b>War Against the Pure</b> for <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b> has some very interesting shifters that could make for good antagonists or agendad NPCs. The PCs are tracking a slasher, only to discover it is one of the Colony, a Werecat who hunts humans with low Morality, but must kill one per month or go mad...and she has no way to know if a human is evil or not, she can only kill a human and hope. Or the wereroaches who send spirit eggs into food all around them and make more wereroaches, or those fishmen that live in isolated villiages. Good stuff. <b>World of Darkness: Slasher</b> should be very useful in a Geist game if you want a more mundane slasher. I really, really like <b>Summoners</b> for Mage, it is a great book I have used a lot despite never having run Mage. The Men in Black are delicious answers to the question of why bother with a Masquerade...Oh just let the PCs try and fight them. The Numbers Stations section of that book is rather interesting as well, and the book is one of the few with Cthonians in it. Also the Abyssal entities which are, for my money, the scariest things in New WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T01:26:29-07:00","id":150106,"title":"","content":"Everything Baron said. <br /> Another note on Detroit, the elmwood cemetary is over 150 years old, and the Battle of Bloody Run was fought on the grounds of what would become the cemetary. Natives fighting in Pontiac's rebellion fought and defeated a British ambushing force. <br /> <br /> Also, the currently standing Ft. Wayne was apparently built directly on top of a Native burial ground. Go figure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T19:03:32-07:00","id":150948,"title":"","content":"Holy crap, that blew up fast. Just gonna post the notes so I don't forget - I think I just got a to-do list of things to look into!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Government knows about Sin-eaters and covers it up<br /> - Urban Decay as a theme?<br /> - Vast salt mines under Detroit<br /> - Map of detroit<br /> - A big bad that can't be thwacked<br /> - Agenda'd NPCs<br /> - WoD Slashers<br /> - Elmwood Cemetary is very old<br /> - Ft Wayne<br /> - Illitch Family instead of Tengu corp </div> </div> </div>My quick thoughts on whats been said so far:<br /> <br /> Not sure how to use Urban Decay as a theme yet, although I think it's going to be eventually unavoidable that the players will find themselves in abandoned buildings and the like. This is one of those things where the idea is just so alien to me that I don't think I can write it well, but I may try.<br /> <br /> Salt mines under Detroit? Gonna have to look into that. Sounds like either a great locale or a plot hook suggestion. I'm going to try and keep my planned stories separate from the setting document (so other people can use it without running the same game - unless they want to) but perhaps I'll suggest a few plot hooks.<br /> <br /> I think a map of Detroit is in order - especially if I can find one that shows areas and neighborhoods rather than just streets. I'll have to see what I can find.<br /> <br /> As for the big bad - I'm gonna avoid mixing in any more systems at this point - I'll have a look at Slashers and antagonists, but I want to hold on to the theme of Geist as much as possible for theme purposes of the setting. Anyone using the setting for their game can add on other systems - but I'd prefer they were added on after the fact. Only Inferno will truly get more than a cameo in the basic setting - the god machine shouldn't be a real player; its just a framing for why the city is what it is in the grande scheme of things. Anyone who pits the players against the GM should be prepared to fundamentally alter the entire setting. So far a Kerberos of some sort seems like the best option - possibly one that is corrupted and able to effect the mortal world some how.<br /> <br /> I like the Agenda'd NPCs idea. Between the mortal gangs that already live in Detroit, the Krewes that will be written up and the police, I already have factions that can be used for this. I'll try to add more groups for this express purpose.<br /> <br /> Elmwood cemetary seems like an excellent haunt for one of the more powerful Krewes, as does Ft. Wayne. I'm gonna try to come up with descriptions of these locales. The cemetary especially seems like a likely location to host flesh fairs that would be very unique to Detroit. <br /> <br /> The Illitch Family seems a very good replacement for my Tengu corp - or even a competitor if I change my mind about bringing the GM in as a major player in the game.<br /> <br /> Huzzah! Time to go look up maps of Detroits neighborhoods! I may even pin one to my wall - I'm sure my friends and loved ones will think I'm a conspiracy theorist by the time I'm done. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T19:30:39-07:00","id":158577,"title":"","content":"Quick update: added a simple map and set about describing about half the city. Still a work in progress, but slowly getting more fleshed out.<br /> <br /> If anyone thinks my description of an area isn't fitting, I'm all ears. I'm going by heresay mostly, and I'd love input from those that might know better than me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}